  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "S. Hariharan vs The Food Inspector on 2 November, 2016 Author: P.N. Prakash Bench: P.N. Prakash In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 02.11.2016 Coram: The Hon'Ble Mr. Justice P.N. Prakash Crl.O.P. No.9009 of 2011 & M.P. No.1 of 2011 1 S. Hariharan 2 Narasus Coffee Company 16 Court Road Johnsonpet Salem 636 007 Petitioners vs. The Food Inspector Tiruppur City Municipal Corporation Tiruppur 638 604 Responde Criminal Original Petition filed under Section 482, Cr.P.C. seeking to call for the reco For petitioners Mr. K.V. Sridharan For respondent Mr. C. Emalias Additional Public Prosecutor Order",
    "facts": "This Criminal Original Petition has been filed to call for the records in C.C. No.324 of 2009 on the file of the Judicial Magistrate Court No.II, Tiruppur and quash the proceedings initiated against the petitioners as abuse of process of Court. 2 The factual matrix of the case is as under: 2.1 The first petitioner is a retail seller/vendor at Tiruppur and the second petitioner is a company manufacturing coffee powder. While so, the respondent, viz., the Food Inspector, visited the premises of the first petitioner and lifted samples of coffee powder on 09.01.2008 and sent the same to the Public Analyst. The Public Analyst found certain deficiencies in the analysed sample and the opinion of the Public S. Hariharan vs The Food Inspector on 2 November, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/108044835/ 1 Analyst in his report dated 06.02.2008 is as follows: \u0013Opinion: I am of the opinion that the sample is adulterated since the sample found to contain coffee husk which shall be free from this sample as per Appendix B to the PFA Rule, 1955. Also the sample is found to be misbranded since it is not labelled in accordance with the requirements of Section 2 (ix),(a),(e) and (k) of the PFA Act, 1954 and also Appendix/A.08.01 (3) of the PFA Rule, 1955.\u0014 2.2 Thereafter, the respondent filed a complaint before the Judicial Magistrate Court No.II, Tiruppur, for offences under the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 against Hariharan (A1), M. Paulraj (A2) and Narasu's Coffee Company (A3) and the same was taken on file on 07.12.2009. A copy of the report of the Public Analyst was served on the petitioners as contemplated under Section 13(2) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, on 12.12.2009, giving liberty to them to dispute the same within ten days from the date of receipt thereof.",
    "arguments": "2.3 Be that as it may, the petitioners have challenged the entire prosecution on the short ground that the prosecution itself has been launched after the shelf life of the coffee powder. The learned counsel for the petitioners submitted that from the Public Analyst's report, it is evident that the coffee powder was manufactured and packed in January 2008 and that the packet carries a printing \u0013BEST BEFORE 4 MONTHS FROM PACKAGING\u0014. Relying upon this, the learned counsel for the petitioners submitted that the complaint should have been filed within four months from January 2008, whereas, admittedly, the complaint has been filed by the respondent only in 2009, which is after the shelf life of the coffee powder.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2.3 Be that as it may, the petitioners have challenged the entire prosecution on the short ground that the prosecution itself has been launched after the shelf life of the coffee powder. The learned counsel for the petitioners submitted that from the Public Analyst's report, it is evident that the coffee powder was manufactured and packed in January 2008 and that the packet carries a printing \u0013BEST BEFORE 4 MONTHS FROM PACKAGING\u0014. Relying upon this, the learned counsel for the petitioners submitted that the complaint should have been filed within four months from January 2008, whereas, admittedly, the complaint has been filed by the respondent only in 2009, which is after the shelf life of the coffee powder.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
